WEBVTT

00:00:00.103 --> 00:00:05.750
Welcome to Module 1 of IAN 601 In this module we are
going to build

00:00:05.763 --> 00:00:10.987
the Python foundation that we will use throughout
the course You do not need prior

00:00:11.000 --> 00:00:16.658
programming experience The goal is to work with
small pieces of code understand what

00:00:16.684 --> 00:00:22.310
each line is doing and connect the code to
analytical work A useful

00:00:22.336 --> 00:00:27.444
mental model for this module is simple We start with
data we give that data

00:00:27.457 --> 00:00:32.970
meaningful names we perform calculations or
transformations and then we communicate the result

00:00:33.891 --> 00:00:40.391
That basic pattern appears again and again in
business analytics healthcare analytics data
cleaning visualization

00:00:40.549 --> 00:00:46.327
statistics and machine learning As you move through
the slides try to predict

00:00:46.353 --> 00:00:51.553
the result before you run a Python example Then
change one value and run it

00:00:51.580 --> 00:00:56.948
again That small habit will help you understand the
code instead of only copying it
